IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `taa-core`

-- Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) -- from the seat of the person injured in a transport accident.
--
-- SEAT: the person injured in a transport accident (a road, train or tram accident), and, under "If the person
-- dies", the surviving partner and dependent children of a person who dies as a result of one. "Am I covered? What
-- does a conviction do to my benefits? By when must I claim, and by when must the Commission decide? How much are my
-- weekly payments in the first 18 months and after, and when do they stop? What impairment benefit do I get? Which
-- medical and like expenses are paid? Can I sue for damages, and for how much? What does my family get if I die?"
-- Each question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in
-- taa-core.l4; this module turns plain answers into the core's inputs and restates no rule.
--
-- FIGURES: the Act's dollar amounts are varied every 1 July (s 61) and no notice of the varied amounts is
-- deposited, so a question that needs one asks for the current figure, which the Transport Accident Commission
-- publishes; each @desc gives the figure the Act prints.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) -- the injured person's questions`

§§ `Am I covered (ss 35-42)`

@export Am I entitled to compensation from the Transport Accident Commission for my injury in a transport accident (ss 35-42 of the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic))? A transport accident is an incident directly caused by driving a motor car or motor vehicle, a railway train or a tram. Answers yes also where the Commission may pay under s 36 and you say it is satisfied.
GIVEN `where my accident happened` IS A `Where the accident occurred` @desc Did the accident happen in Victoria, in another Australian State or Territory, or outside Australia?
      `my accident involved a registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident outside Victoria: did it involve a motor vehicle registered in Victoria (or usually kept here and not registered elsewhere)?
      `I was a resident of Victoria at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a resident of Victoria at the time of the accident?
      `I was the driver of or a passenger in that registered vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident outside Victoria: were you the driver of, or a passenger in, that registered motor vehicle?
      `the Commission is satisfied I was likely to live in Victoria for six months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident outside Victoria, if you were neither a resident nor its driver or passenger: is the Commission satisfied you were likely to live in Victoria for at least six months after the accident (s 36)?
      `I am entitled to workers' compensation for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to compensation for this injury under the workers' compensation Acts (Accident Compensation Act 1985 or Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013) or one of the other schemes in s 37 (CFA, SES, police assistance, emergency management, juries, schools), or an interstate equivalent?
      `my accident involved` IS A `What the accident involved` @desc Did the accident involve a motor vehicle or pedal cycle (other than a recreation vehicle), a recreation vehicle only (a low-fee registered motor cycle), or a railway train or tram?
      `the accident was reported` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accident reported to the police (or, for a train or tram, to its operator)?
      `the Commission excused the failure to report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was not reported: has the Commission decided that, in all the circumstances, the failure should be excused (s 39(2))?
      `my part in a race or speed trial` IS A `Part in an organised race or speed trial` @desc Did the accident happen in an organised race or speed trial (or a test for one), and if so, were you a driver, passenger or rider taking part; a spectator, official, organiser or helper; or a cyclist taking part who was hit by a vehicle not taking part?
      `the race was run under the Road Safety Act and certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was the race run under rules requiring the Road Safety Act 1986 to be followed, and certified in writing by the Commission (s 41(1A))?
      `the accident involved an unregistered vehicle on private land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accident involve driving a never-registered motor vehicle, with no transport accident charge paid, on private land (land that is not a highway and that the public may not enter without permission) (s 41A)?
      `I owned an uninsured vehicle driven on private land in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the owner of a motor vehicle, whose transport accident charge had not been paid for at least 12 months, that was being driven on private land in the accident (s 41B)?
      `I have recovered, settled or sued under another place's law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory, have you been paid, awarded, settled, accepted a payment into court, had a claim accepted, or started an action for damages, for this accident (s 42(2))?
      `the Commission is liable to me under that law through s 94(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: is the Commission itself liable to pay you under that other law, through its indemnity under s 94(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to compensation for my transport accident injury` `where my accident happened` `my accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `I was a resident of Victoria at the time` `I was the driver of or a passenger in that registered vehicle` `the Commission is satisfied I was likely to live in Victoria for six months` `I am entitled to workers' compensation for this injury` `my accident involved` `the accident was reported` `the Commission excused the failure to report` `my part in a race or speed trial` `the race was run under the Road Safety Act and certified` `the accident involved an unregistered vehicle on private land` `I owned an uninsured vehicle driven on private land in the accident` `I have recovered, settled or sued under another place's law` `the Commission is liable to me under that law through s 94(1)` MEANS
    `ss 35-42 -- the Commission is liable, or may pay, compensation for the injury`
        `where my accident happened`
        `my accident involved a registered motor vehicle`
        `I was a resident of Victoria at the time`
        `I was the driver of or a passenger in that registered vehicle`
        `the Commission is satisfied I was likely to live in Victoria for six months`
        `I am entitled to workers' compensation for this injury`
        `my accident involved`
        `the accident was reported`
        `the Commission excused the failure to report`
        `my part in a race or speed trial`
        `the race was run under the Road Safety Act and certified`
        `the accident involved an unregistered vehicle on private land`
        `I owned an uninsured vehicle driven on private land in the accident`
        `I have recovered, settled or sued under another place's law`
        `the Commission is liable to me under that law through s 94(1)`

§§ `What a conviction or the circumstances of my driving do (ss 39(3), 40)`

-- The three questions share their inputs and the core's one rule.
GIVEN `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my conviction` IS A `Conviction`
      `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER
      `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my licence` IS A `Licence at the time`
      `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a conviction does`
`what my conviction or circumstances do` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` MEANS
    `ss 39(3), 40 -- what a conviction or the circumstances do` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of`

@export What share of my loss of earnings compensation (ss 44, 45) is still payable after a drink-driving, drug-driving or other driving conviction, or because I was unlicensed or my vehicle's transport accident charge was unpaid (ss 39(3), 40)? 1 is all of it, 0 none.
GIVEN `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident?
      `my conviction` IS A `Conviction` @desc Which offence, if any, were you convicted of in respect of the accident or your driving at that time? For the combined alcohol and drugs offence (Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bc) or (j)) a finding of guilt without a conviction also counts (s 40(3A), (4B)); for every other offence only a conviction counts. Choose no conviction if none.
      `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc The concentration of alcohol the court found, in grams per 100 millilitres of blood (or per 210 litres of breath), e.g. 0.08; 0 if none
      `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the Commission that the alcohol or drugs (or the concentration) did not contribute in any way to the accident?
      `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the driver of, or a passenger in, a motor vehicle you owned whose transport accident charge for the period had not been paid (s 40(1)(b))?
      `my licence` IS A `Licence at the time` @desc If you were driving: did you hold a licence for that class of vehicle, had you never held one (a learner with a fully licensed driver beside you counts as holding one), was it suspended or cancelled, or had it not been renewed for at least 3 years?
      `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the driver of or a passenger in a vehicle used in an indictable offence, stealing a vehicle, escaping arrest or intentionally injuring someone, and were you convicted of that offence (s 40(1)(d))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What share of my loss of earnings compensation is payable after a conviction` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` MEANS
    (`what my conviction or circumstances do` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of`)'s `the share of loss of earnings compensation payable (ss 44, 45)`

@export After a driving conviction, can I still be paid an impairment benefit and weekly payments for loss of earning capacity (ss 47, 49, 50, 51), under ss 39(3) and 40?
GIVEN `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident?
      `my conviction` IS A `Conviction` @desc Which offence, if any, were you convicted of in respect of the accident or your driving at that time? For the combined alcohol and drugs offence (Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bc) or (j)) a finding of guilt without a conviction also counts (s 40(3A), (4B)); for every other offence only a conviction counts. Choose no conviction if none.
      `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc The concentration of alcohol the court found, in grams per 100 millilitres of blood (or per 210 litres of breath), e.g. 0.08; 0 if none
      `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the Commission that the alcohol or drugs (or the concentration) did not contribute in any way to the accident?
      `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the driver of, or a passenger in, a motor vehicle you owned whose transport accident charge for the period had not been paid (s 40(1)(b))?
      `my licence` IS A `Licence at the time` @desc If you were driving: did you hold a licence for that class of vehicle, had you never held one, was it suspended or cancelled, or had it not been renewed for at least 3 years?
      `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a vehicle used in an indictable offence and convicted of that offence (s 40(1)(d))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I still be paid impairment and earning capacity benefits after a conviction` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` MEANS
    (`what my conviction or circumstances do` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of`)'s `impairment and earning capacity benefits are payable (ss 47, 49, 50, 51)`

@export After a conviction, can I be paid anything other than medical and like expenses under s 60 (s 39(3): murder, manslaughter, Crimes Act s 5A, or culpable or dangerous driving under Crimes Act s 318(1) or 319(1))?
GIVEN `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident?
      `my conviction` IS A `Conviction` @desc Which offence, if any, were you convicted of? Choose no conviction if none.
      `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc The concentration of alcohol the court found, in grams per 100 millilitres; 0 if none
      `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the Commission that the alcohol or drugs did not contribute in any way to the accident?
      `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a vehicle you owned whose transport accident charge had not been paid?
      `my licence` IS A `Licence at the time` @desc If you were driving: the state of your licence for that class of vehicle
      `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a vehicle used in an indictable offence and convicted of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be paid anything other than medical and like expenses after a conviction` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of` MEANS
    (`what my conviction or circumstances do` `I was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `my conviction` `my blood or breath alcohol concentration` `I satisfy the Commission it did not contribute` `I owned the vehicle and its charge was unpaid` `my licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence I am convicted of`)'s `compensation other than under s 60 is payable`

§§ `The claim, the decision and review (ss 64, 66, 68, 70, 77)`

DECLARE `Claiming as` IS ONE OF
    `the injured person`
    `a dependant or surviving partner of a person who died`

GIVEN `I am claiming as` IS A `Claiming as`
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `my injury showed itself at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day my claim time runs from` `I am claiming as` `the day of the accident` `my injury showed itself at the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day of the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `I am claiming as`
    WHEN `the injured person` THEN
        IF `my injury showed itself at the accident` THEN `the day of the accident` ELSE `the day my injury first showed itself`
    WHEN `a dependant or surviving partner of a person who died` THEN `the day of the death`

@export By what day must I make my claim for compensation to the Transport Accident Commission (s 68(1), (3))? One year after the accident or death (or after an injury that did not show at first manifests itself); if you were under 18 at the accident, the later of the day before you turn 21 and 3 years after the accident.
GIVEN `I am claiming as` IS A `Claiming as` @desc Are you claiming as the injured person, or as a dependant or surviving partner of a person who died?
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `my injury showed itself at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the injured person: did the injury show itself at the time of the accident?
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc If not: the day the injury first manifested itself (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc For a dependant or surviving partner: the day the person died (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `I was under 18 at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you (the injured person, or the dependent child claiming) under 18 at the time of the accident?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I make my claim` `I am claiming as` `the day of the accident` `my injury showed itself at the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day of the death` `I was under 18 at the accident` `my date of birth` MEANS
    `s 68(1), (3) -- the last day to claim`
        (`the day my claim time runs from` `I am claiming as` `the day of the accident` `my injury showed itself at the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day of the death`)
        `the day of the accident`
        `I was under 18 at the accident`
        (`the day of attaining age` 21 `my date of birth`)

@export I make (or made) my claim on a certain day: is it in time, or can the Commission still accept it because it considers there are reasonable grounds for the delay (s 68(2): up to 3 years after the accident, death or first manifestation)?
GIVEN `I am claiming as` IS A `Claiming as` @desc Are you claiming as the injured person, or as a dependant or surviving partner of a person who died?
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `my injury showed itself at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the injured person: did the injury show itself at the time of the accident?
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc If not: the day the injury first manifested itself (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc For a dependant or surviving partner: the day the person died (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `I was under 18 at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under 18 at the time of the accident?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim is (or was) lodged with the Commission (ISO date)
      `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for my delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late claim: does the Commission consider there are reasonable grounds for the delay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my claim made in time` `I am claiming as` `the day of the accident` `my injury showed itself at the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day of the death` `I was under 18 at the accident` `my date of birth` `the day I make my claim` `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for my delay` MEANS
    `s 68 -- the claim is made in time`
        (`the day my claim time runs from` `I am claiming as` `the day of the accident` `my injury showed itself at the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day of the death`)
        `the day of the accident`
        `I was under 18 at the accident`
        (`the day of attaining age` 21 `my date of birth`)
        `the day I make my claim`
        `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for my delay`

@export By what day must the Transport Accident Commission accept or reject my claim, or ask me (or someone else) for more information or a medical examination (s 70(1))? If it does none of these, the claim is taken to be rejected.
GIVEN `the day the Commission received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission received your claim (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must the Commission respond to my claim` `the day the Commission received my claim` MEANS
    `s 70(1) -- the last day for the Commission to respond to the claim` `the day the Commission received my claim`

@export The Commission asked me for further information or a medical examination: by what day must it then accept or reject my claim (s 70(2))? The later of 14 days after it receives the information or result and 21 days after it received the claim.
GIVEN `the day the Commission received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission received your claim (ISO date)
      `the day the Commission received the information or result` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission received the further information or the result of the medical examination (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must the Commission decide my claim after asking me for more` `the day the Commission received my claim` `the day the Commission received the information or result` MEANS
    `s 70(2) -- the last day to decide after a request to the claimant` `the day the Commission received my claim` `the day the Commission received the information or result`

@export The Commission asked me for further information or to attend a medical examination: by what day must I comply, so my claim does not lapse (s 70(4))? 28 days after the request, or a longer period the Commission allows.
GIVEN `the day the Commission made the request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission made the request (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I comply with the Commission's request` `the day the Commission made the request` MEANS
    `s 70(4) -- the last day to comply with a request` `the day the Commission made the request`

@export The Commission did not decide my claim in time, so it is taken to be rejected: by what day can I apply to the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review (s 70(3)(b))? 12 months after the end of the Commission's time.
GIVEN `the day the Commission received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission received your claim (ISO date)
      `the Commission asked me for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission ask you for further information or a medical examination?
      `the day the Commission received the information or result` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it received the information or the examination result (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day can I apply to the Tribunal after my claim is taken to be rejected` `the day the Commission received my claim` `the Commission asked me for more information` `the day the Commission received the information or result` MEANS
    `s 70(3)(b) -- the last day to apply to the Tribunal after a deemed rejection`
        (IF `the Commission asked me for more information`
         THEN `s 70(2) -- the last day to decide after a request to the claimant` `the day the Commission received my claim` `the day the Commission received the information or result`
         ELSE `s 70(1) -- the last day for the Commission to respond to the claim` `the day the Commission received my claim`)

@export By what day can I apply to the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review of a decision of the Transport Accident Commission (s 77(1A))? 12 months after you became aware of it, or 3 months after the Commission's decision on a pre-issue review under the No Fault Dispute Resolution Protocols if that is later. Answers nothing for a decision about an interim impairment benefit, which cannot be reviewed (s 77(2)).
GIVEN `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about paying (or not paying) an interim impairment benefit under s 47(3A)?
      `the day I became aware of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware of the decision (ISO date)
      `I applied for a pre-issue review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for a pre-issue review of the decision under the No Fault Dispute Resolution Protocols?
      `the day the Commission notified me of its pre-issue review decision` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day the Commission notified you of its decision on that application (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day can I apply to the Tribunal for review of a decision` `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit` `the day I became aware of the decision` `I applied for a pre-issue review` `the day the Commission notified me of its pre-issue review decision` MEANS
    `s 77(1A) -- the last day to apply to the Tribunal for review` `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit` `the day I became aware of the decision` `I applied for a pre-issue review` `the day the Commission notified me of its pre-issue review decision`

@export I was the driver and the Commission served me a notice asking for a report of the accident: by what day must I make the report in the prescribed form (s 64(1), (3))? 28 days after receiving the notice. Not doing so does not affect your right to compensation (s 64(4)).
GIVEN `the day I received the Commission's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commission's notice (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I make the accident report` `the day I received the Commission's notice` MEANS
    `s 64(1) -- the last day to make the report` `the day I received the Commission's notice`

@export I did not make the report in time: by what day can I pay the $50 penalty so that no further proceedings are taken against me (s 66(1)(a))? 14 days after the 28 days end, or later if the Commission allows.
GIVEN `the day I received the Commission's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commission's notice (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day can I pay the penalty for not reporting` `the day I received the Commission's notice` MEANS
    `s 66(1)(a) -- the last day to pay the penalty` `the day I received the Commission's notice`

§§ `Weekly payments for loss of earnings in the first 18 months (ss 43-46)`

-- A situation: only for a person who was an earner (in work in the 8 weeks, or 13 of the 52 weeks, or 26 of the
-- 104 weeks, before the accident, s 3(2)) and lost earnings.

@export For a given day, is the Commission liable to pay me for loss of earnings (ss 43, 44(4), 45(6), 46(2))? Not for the first five days on which you lose earnings (unless the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship), and not after the first 18 months, unless the Commission's 18-month review is late.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury first manifested itself; the accident day if it showed then (ISO date)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
      `the number of earlier days on which I lost earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before this one, from the accident (or the day the injury showed itself, if later), did you lose earnings because of the injury?
      `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the first five days: is the Commission satisfied you would suffer acute financial hardship without a payment (s 43(2))?
      `the Commission's 18-month review was not completed in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Commission's review of your entitlement to earning capacity payments still not completed 18 months after the accident (s 46(2))?
      `the day the review was completed` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it was completed (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the Commission liable to pay me for loss of earnings on this day` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day` `the number of earlier days on which I lost earnings` `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship` `the Commission's 18-month review was not completed in time` `the day the review was completed` MEANS
    `ss 43, 44(4), 45(6) -- the day is in the period of entitlement`
        (`the day the time counts from` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself`)
        `the day`
        `the number of earlier days on which I lost earnings`
        `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship`
        `the Commission's 18-month review was not completed in time`
        `the day the review was completed`

@export How much is my weekly payment if I cannot work at all because of my transport accident injury, in the first 18 months (s 44)? The greater of 80% of your pre-accident weekly earnings and the minimum for your dependants, but not more than the maximum or 100% of your pre-accident weekly earnings. Enter the Commission's current figures; the Act prints $304, $85, $27 and $621.
GIVEN `my pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident weekly earnings: the weekly average of your gross earnings in the 12 months before the accident (or a shorter period if you had not been earning that long, or since a promotion or new job), in dollars (s 4)
      `the number of my dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people would, but for the injury, depend on you wholly, mainly or in part for economic support?
      `I am already paid for an earlier transport accident` IS AN `Earlier accident payment` @desc Are you already receiving weekly payments for loss of earnings for an earlier transport accident, under s 44 (not working at all) or s 45 (partly)?
      `my s 44 weekly payment for the earlier accident` IS A NUMBER @desc If under s 44: that weekly payment, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `my pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident` IS A NUMBER @desc If under s 45: your pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `the current s 44(2)(b) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for s 44(2)(b), the minimum with no dependants (the Act prints $304, varied each 1 July)
      `the current amount for one dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for one dependant, s 44(2)(c)(ii) (the Act prints $85)
      `the current amount for each other dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for each other dependant, s 44(2)(c)(iii) (the Act prints $27)
      `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly payment, s 44(3)(a) (the Act prints $621)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment for total loss of earnings` `my pre-accident weekly earnings` `the number of my dependants` `I am already paid for an earlier transport accident` `my s 44 weekly payment for the earlier accident` `my pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident` `the current s 44(2)(b) amount` `the current amount for one dependant` `the current amount for each other dependant` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` MEANS
    `s 44 -- the weekly payment for total loss of earnings`
        (`Weekly payment figures` WITH
            `the base amount`                     IS `the current s 44(2)(b) amount`
            `the amount for one dependant`        IS `the current amount for one dependant`
            `the amount for each other dependant` IS `the current amount for each other dependant`
            `the maximum`                         IS `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum`)
        `my pre-accident weekly earnings`
        `the number of my dependants`
        `I am already paid for an earlier transport accident`
        `my s 44 weekly payment for the earlier accident`
        `my pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident`

@export How much is my weekly payment if my transport accident injury means I lose part of my earnings, in the first 18 months (s 45)? If you are working: the greater of 85% of the drop in your earnings and the dependants' minimum less your earnings, capped. If you are not working: as for total loss. Enter the Commission's current figures; the Act prints $304, $85, $27 and $621.
GIVEN `my pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident weekly earnings, in dollars (s 4); if you were already paid for an earlier transport accident, those before the earlier accident (s 45(5A))
      `the number of my dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people would, but for the injury, depend on you wholly, mainly or in part for economic support?
      `I am employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed (working) in the week?
      `my earnings this week` IS A NUMBER @desc If employed: your earnings in the week the payment is for, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `the current s 45 minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for the minimum with no dependants, s 45(2)(b) (the Act prints $304, varied each 1 July)
      `the current amount for one dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for one dependant (the Act prints $85)
      `the current amount for each other dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for each other dependant (the Act prints $27)
      `the current s 45 maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly payment, s 45(3)(a) and (5)(a) (the Act prints $621)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment for partial loss of earnings` `my pre-accident weekly earnings` `the number of my dependants` `I am employed` `my earnings this week` `the current s 45 minimum` `the current amount for one dependant` `the current amount for each other dependant` `the current s 45 maximum` MEANS
    `s 45 -- the weekly payment for partial loss of earnings`
        (`Weekly payment figures` WITH
            `the base amount`                     IS `the current s 45 minimum`
            `the amount for one dependant`        IS `the current amount for one dependant`
            `the amount for each other dependant` IS `the current amount for each other dependant`
            `the maximum`                         IS `the current s 45 maximum`)
        `my pre-accident weekly earnings`
        `the number of my dependants`
        `I am employed`
        `my earnings this week`

@export I am self-employed and cannot work at all: how much is my interim weekly payment until the Commission works out my pre-accident weekly earnings, for at most the first 12 weeks (s 45AA)? 75% of the current maximum weekly payment (the Act prints $621).
GIVEN `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly payment, s 44(3)(a) (the Act prints $621, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my interim weekly payment as a self-employed person` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` MEANS
    `s 45AA -- the interim weekly payment to a self-employed earner` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum`

@export I am a seasonal earner (fruit-picking, ski instruction and the like): by what day must I give the Commission my written election to be paid week by week on my seasonal pattern (s 45AC(4))? 14 days after you become entitled to a payment; the Commission may waive this.
GIVEN `the day I became entitled to a loss of earnings payment` IS A DATE @desc The day you became entitled to receive a payment under s 44 or 45 (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I elect to be paid on a seasonal basis` `the day I became entitled to a loss of earnings payment` MEANS
    `s 45AC(4) -- the last day for a seasonal earner's election` `the day I became entitled to a loss of earnings payment`

§§ `Weekly payments for loss of earning capacity after 18 months (ss 49-53)`

-- A situation: only for a person whose injury still limits their capacity to earn after 18 months.

@export How much is my weekly payment for loss of earning capacity after the first 18 months (ss 49, 50, 52)? Total loss: the greater of 80% of your pre-accident earning capacity and the dependants' minimum, capped. Partial loss: nothing if the loss is under 10%; otherwise the greater of 85% of the loss and the minimum less your remaining capacity, capped. Enter the Commission's current figures; the Act prints $270, $76, $25 and $504.
GIVEN `my loss of earning capacity` IS A `Loss of earning capacity` @desc Have you lost all your capacity to earn, or part of it?
      `my pre-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident earning capacity as the Commission determined it: the weekly amount you could earn before the accident in work reasonably available to you, less income tax, in dollars (s 49(5), (5A))
      `my post-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc For a partial loss: the weekly amount, less income tax, the Commission determined you can still earn in work reasonably available to you, in dollars (s 50(5)); 0 for a total loss
      `the number of my dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people would, but for the injury, depend on you wholly, mainly or in part for economic support?
      `the current s 49 minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for the minimum with no dependants, s 49(2)(b) and s 50(2)(b) (the Act prints $270, varied each 1 July)
      `the current amount for one dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for one dependant (the Act prints $76)
      `the current amount for each other dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for each other dependant (the Act prints $25)
      `the current s 49 maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly payment, s 49(3)(a) and s 50(3)(a) (the Act prints $504)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment for loss of earning capacity` `my loss of earning capacity` `my pre-accident earning capacity` `my post-accident earning capacity` `the number of my dependants` `the current s 49 minimum` `the current amount for one dependant` `the current amount for each other dependant` `the current s 49 maximum` MEANS
    `ss 49, 50, 52 -- the weekly payment for loss of earning capacity`
        (`Weekly payment figures` WITH
            `the base amount`                     IS `the current s 49 minimum`
            `the amount for one dependant`        IS `the current amount for one dependant`
            `the amount for each other dependant` IS `the current amount for each other dependant`
            `the maximum`                         IS `the current s 49 maximum`)
        `my loss of earning capacity`
        `my pre-accident earning capacity`
        `my post-accident earning capacity`
        `the number of my dependants`

@export I was not an earner when I was injured (and not a minor): how much is my weekly payment for loss of earning capacity after the first 18 months (s 51)? The ss 49-50 amount less A x B / (C - D): A that amount, B the years before pension age you would likely not have worked, C pension age, D your age. Answers nothing at or over pension age. Enter the Commission's current figures; the Act prints $270, $76, $25 and $504.
GIVEN `my loss of earning capacity` IS A `Loss of earning capacity` @desc Have you lost all your capacity to earn, or part of it?
      `my pre-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount, less income tax, the Commission determines you could have earned before the accident in work reasonably available to you (or, if it cannot be determined, Victorian average weekly earnings, s 49(5A)), in dollars
      `my post-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc For a partial loss: the weekly amount, less income tax, you can still earn, in dollars; 0 for a total loss
      `the number of my dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people depend on you wholly, mainly or in part for economic support?
      `the years before pension age I would likely not have worked` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years before you reach pension age during which you were reasonably likely not to be employed (as the Commission assesses it)
      `my pension age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), in years (67 for most people)
      `my age in whole years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `the current s 49 minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for the minimum with no dependants (the Act prints $270)
      `the current amount for one dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for one dependant (the Act prints $76)
      `the current amount for each other dependant` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for each other dependant (the Act prints $25)
      `the current s 49 maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum weekly payment (the Act prints $504)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment for loss of earning capacity as a non-earner` `my loss of earning capacity` `my pre-accident earning capacity` `my post-accident earning capacity` `the number of my dependants` `the years before pension age I would likely not have worked` `my pension age` `my age in whole years` `the current s 49 minimum` `the current amount for one dependant` `the current amount for each other dependant` `the current s 49 maximum` MEANS
    `s 51 -- the weekly payment for loss of earning capacity of a non-earner`
        (`How much is my weekly payment for loss of earning capacity` `my loss of earning capacity` `my pre-accident earning capacity` `my post-accident earning capacity` `the number of my dependants` `the current s 49 minimum` `the current amount for one dependant` `the current amount for each other dependant` `the current s 49 maximum`)
        `the years before pension age I would likely not have worked`
        `my pension age`
        `my age in whole years`

@export Have my weekly payments stopped on a given day because of my age, prison, damages, the 3-year limit or the total paid (s 53)? Loss of earning capacity payments stop 3 years after the injury showed itself (21 for a minor) or when the total paid reaches the limit, unless your impairment is 50% or more. Yes means stopped; no means s 53 does not stop them. Enter the Commission's current s 53(3)(b) figure (the Act prints $99 220).
GIVEN `the payments I am asking about` IS A `Kind of weekly payment` @desc Which weekly payments: loss of earnings (s 44 or 45, the first 18 months), loss of earning capacity (s 49, 50 or 51, after 18 months), or the safety net income benefit (s 54A)?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury first manifested itself; the accident day if it showed then (ISO date)
      `the day I reach my retiring age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach the normal retiring age for workers in your occupation at the time of the injury or, if there is none, your age pension age (ISO date)
      `I was a minor when my injury showed itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under 18 and not an earner when the injury first manifested itself?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
      `I am in prison on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in prison serving a sentence of imprisonment on that day?
      `my pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before that day, were damages for your pecuniary loss (loss of earnings or earning capacity) for this injury settled or awarded (s 93)?
      `the total paid to me under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54` IS A NUMBER @desc The total the Commission has paid you so far for this injury in weekly payments for loss of earnings and earning capacity (and minors' benefits), in dollars
      `the current s 53(3)(b) limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 53(3)(b) limit on the total paid (the Act prints $99 220, varied each 1 July)
      `my impairment` IS AN `Impairment for s 53(4), (5)` @desc Has the Commission determined your degree of impairment at 50% or more; or, if it had not been determined 3 years after the accident, is it likely to be 50% or more; or neither?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Have my weekly payments stopped on this day` `the payments I am asking about` `the day` `the day my injury first showed itself` `the day I reach my retiring age` `I was a minor when my injury showed itself` `my date of birth` `I am in prison on the day` `my pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded` `the total paid to me under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54` `the current s 53(3)(b) limit` `my impairment` MEANS
    `s 53 -- the weekly payments are stopped on the day`
        `the payments I am asking about`
        `the day`
        `the day my injury first showed itself`
        `the day I reach my retiring age`
        `I was a minor when my injury showed itself`
        (`the day of attaining age` 21 `my date of birth`)
        `I am in prison on the day`
        `my pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded`
        `the total paid to me under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54`
        `the current s 53(3)(b) limit`
        `my impairment`

@export I receive weekly payments for loss of earning capacity: by what day must I give the Commission my statement of earnings after an anniversary of my first payment (ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5))? Two months after the anniversary.
GIVEN `the day of my first payment` IS A DATE @desc The day you first received a weekly payment for loss of earning capacity for this accident (ISO date)
      `which anniversary` IS A NUMBER @desc Which anniversary of that day: 1 for the first, 2 for the second, and so on
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I give my statement of earnings` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary` MEANS
    `s 49(4) -- the last day for the statement of earnings` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary`

§§ `The safety net income benefit for a severe injury (s 54A)`

-- A situation: only for a person with a severe injury and an impairment of 50% or more whose job has ended.

@export I have a severe injury and an impairment of 50% or more, and my job has ended: am I entitled to the safety net income benefit (s 54A)?
GIVEN `my severe injury` IS A `Severe injury head` @desc Is your injury a significant acquired brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia, amputation of a limb, burns to more than 50% of the body, another injury the regulations specify, or none of these?
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment as the Commission determined it, in per cent
      `I would otherwise be entitled to earning capacity payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you otherwise be entitled to weekly payments for loss of earning capacity under s 49, 50 or 51?
      `my employment ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment been terminated, or can you no longer sustain your self-employment?
      `I unreasonably refuse rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you unreasonably refuse to take part in a rehabilitation or vocational rehabilitation program the Commission approved?
      `an offer of suitable employment` IS AN `Offer of suitable employment` @desc Have you had no reasonable offer of suitable employment; one you did not take up; or one you took up, and that job has since ended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to the safety net income benefit` `my severe injury` `my degree of impairment` `I would otherwise be entitled to earning capacity payments` `my employment ended` `I unreasonably refuse rehabilitation` `an offer of suitable employment` MEANS
    `s 54A -- the person is entitled to the safety net income benefit` `my severe injury` `my degree of impairment` `I would otherwise be entitled to earning capacity payments` `my employment ended` `I unreasonably refuse rehabilitation` `an offer of suitable employment`

@export What is the most my safety net weekly payment can be (s 54A(5))? The lesser of the current s 54A(5)(a) figure (the Act prints $965) and 80% of the greater of your weekly earnings before your job ended and your pre-accident weekly earnings. The Act states only this maximum.
GIVEN `the current s 54A(5)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 54A(5)(a) figure (the Act prints $965, varied each 1 July)
      `my weekly earnings before my job ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-termination weekly earnings: the weekly average of your gross earnings in the 12 months before your post-accident job ended, in dollars
      `my pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident weekly earnings, in dollars (s 4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my safety net weekly payment can be` `the current s 54A(5)(a) amount` `my weekly earnings before my job ended` `my pre-accident weekly earnings` MEANS
    `s 54A(5) -- the most the safety net weekly payment can be` `the current s 54A(5)(a) amount` `my weekly earnings before my job ended` `my pre-accident weekly earnings`

§§ `My degree of impairment and the impairment benefit (ss 46A, 46C, 47)`

@export The assessment of my impairment came to a number with a fraction: what whole percentage is it rounded to (s 46C(2))? To the nearest whole percent; 9.5% becomes 10% and 8.4% becomes 8%.
GIVEN `the assessed number` IS A NUMBER @desc The final degree of impairment the assessment came to, in per cent, e.g. 9.5
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my degree of impairment rounded to` `the assessed number` MEANS
    `s 46C -- rounded to the nearest whole percent` `the assessed number`

@export What degree of impairment does my binaural hearing loss give (s 46A(3))? Under 10% NAL, none; 10% NAL, 10%; more, 10 + 0.278 x (NAL - 10), rounded up.
GIVEN `my binaural hearing loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Your binaural loss of hearing as determined under the National Acoustic Laboratory procedure, in per cent NAL
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What degree of impairment does my hearing loss give` `my binaural hearing loss` MEANS
    `s 46A(3) -- the degree of impairment for binaural hearing loss` `my binaural hearing loss`

@export From what day can the Commission determine my degree of impairment (s 46A(1AA))? Not within 3 months after the accident.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can my degree of impairment be determined` `the day of the accident` MEANS
    `s 46A(1AA) -- the first day the degree of impairment may be determined` `the day of the accident`

@export By what day must I apply in writing for an impairment assessment, if the Commission has neither assessed me nor told me I seem likely to be entitled, so that my impairment is not taken to be 0% (s 46A(1A), (1B))? 6 years after the accident (or after the injury showed itself, if later); for a person under 18 at the accident, 6 years after turning 18.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury first manifested itself; the accident day if it showed then (ISO date)
      `I was a minor at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under 18 and not an earner at the time of the accident?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I apply for an impairment assessment` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `I was a minor at the accident` `my date of birth` MEANS
    `s 46A(1A), (1B) -- the last day of the 6 years`
        (`the day the time counts from` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself`)
        `I was a minor at the accident`
        (`the day of attaining age` 18 `my date of birth`)

@export On a given day, is my degree of impairment taken to be 0%, because 6 years passed with no assessment, no advice that I seem likely to be entitled and no written application from me (s 46A(1A))? Only for a person with an accepted claim (other than one only for death or family benefits).
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury first manifested itself; the accident day if it showed then (ISO date)
      `I was a minor at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under 18 and not an earner at the time of the accident?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO date)
      `I have an accepted claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim within the s 68 time that the Commission accepted (not one only for death benefits or family members' counselling or travel)?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
      `the Commission assessed, advised or received my application in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within the 6 years, did the Commission determine your degree of impairment, advise you that you appear likely to be entitled to an impairment benefit, or receive your written application for an assessment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my degree of impairment taken to be 0%` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` `I was a minor at the accident` `my date of birth` `I have an accepted claim` `the day` `the Commission assessed, advised or received my application in time` MEANS
    `s 46A(1A) -- the degree of impairment is taken to be 0%`
        (`the day the time counts from` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself`)
        `I was a minor at the accident`
        (`the day of attaining age` 18 `my date of birth`)
        `I have an accepted claim`
        `the day`
        `the Commission assessed, advised or received my application in time`

@export How much is my impairment benefit, at the amounts printed in the Act's table (s 47(2))? Nothing for 10% or less; for 11% to 100% the table's amount, e.g. 30% gives $30 000. The printed amounts have been varied every 1 July since 2005 (s 61(2A)), so this is the Act's base, not today's figure: see the next question. Answers nothing over 100%.
GIVEN `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment as the Commission determined it, a whole percentage (s 46C)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my impairment benefit at the Act's printed amounts` `my degree of impairment` MEANS
    `s 47(2) -- the impairment benefit at the printed amounts` `my degree of impairment`

@export How much is my impairment benefit at the Commission's current amounts (s 47(2), varied under s 61(2A))? Enter the current starting amount and amount for each percentage point of the band your degree falls in (bands start at 11, 20, 50, 60, 80, 90 and 100%); for 100%, the amount in the starting amount.
GIVEN `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment as the Commission determined it, a whole percentage (s 46C)
      `the current starting amount for my band` IS A NUMBER @desc The current starting amount for your band (printed: $4 500 for 11-19%, $15 000 for 20-49%, $60 250 for 50-59%, $78 000 for 60-79%, $120 000 for 80-89%, $164 000 for 90-99%, $252 000 for 100%)
      `the current amount for each point in my band` IS A NUMBER @desc The current amount for each percentage point above the band's start (printed: $1000, $1500, $1750, $2000, $4000, $8000; 0 for 100%)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my impairment benefit at the current amounts` `my degree of impairment` `the current starting amount for my band` `the current amount for each point in my band` MEANS
    `s 47(2) -- the impairment benefit with the amounts` `my degree of impairment` `the current starting amount for my band` `the current amount for each point in my band`

§§ `Medical and like expenses (ss 60, 60A)`

@export From what day are my medical and like expenses covered by my application (s 60(1A))? From the accident, if you apply within 3 years after it; otherwise only the 2 years before you apply.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) the application for compensation (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day are my medical and like expenses covered` `the day of the accident` `the day I apply` MEANS
    `s 60(1A) -- the first day of the period for expenses` `the day of the accident` `the day I apply`

@export I was caring for a child, unpaid, in the 30 days before the accident (or I or my partner was pregnant): for how many hours a week can child care be paid, in the first 5 years (s 60(2)(c))? Together with home services, 40 hours a week at most (s 60(2AA)).
GIVEN `my paid employment at the accident` IS A `Paid employment at the accident` @desc At the time of the accident, were you in full-time paid employment of 35 hours or more a week, in paid employment of less than 35 hours a week, or not in paid employment?
      `my hours of paid employment a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If less than 35 hours: how many hours a week of paid employment (0 otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours a week of child care can be paid` `my paid employment at the accident` `my hours of paid employment a week` MEANS
    `s 60(2)(c) -- the most hours of child care a week` `my paid employment at the accident` `my hours of paid employment a week`

@export My child was injured and admitted to hospital: what is the most I can be paid for wages I lost visiting them (s 60(2CA)-(2CD))? Not the first 5 days (unless acute financial hardship); a day at most one-fifth of the current s 44(3)(a) figure; in all at most the current s 60(2CA) figure (the Act prints $621 and $10 000).
GIVEN `the days I lost wages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of wages you lost visiting your child in hospital
      `the wages I lost each day` IS A NUMBER @desc The wages you lost each day, in dollars
      `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the first 5 days: is the Commission satisfied you would suffer acute financial hardship without a payment?
      `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 44(3)(a) figure (the Act prints $621, varied each 1 July)
      `the current s 60(2CA) limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 60(2CA) limit (the Act prints $10 000)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be paid for wages lost visiting my child in hospital` `the days I lost wages` `the wages I lost each day` `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the current s 60(2CA) limit` MEANS
    `s 60(2CA)-(2CD) -- the most paid for a parent's lost wages` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the current s 60(2CA) limit` `the days I lost wages` `the wages I lost each day` `the Commission is satisfied I would suffer acute financial hardship`

@export I went back into hospital (as an inpatient or for day surgery) at least 3 years after the accident: what is the most I can be paid for wages lost during the stay and recovery (s 60A)? Nothing if the hospital stay was less than 3 years after the accident; a day at most one-fifth of the current s 44(3)(a) figure; in all, for the accident, the current s 60A(4) figure (the Act prints $621 and $3500).
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day I went into hospital` IS A DATE @desc The day you first received the hospital services (ISO date)
      `the days I lost wages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of wages you lost while in hospital or recovering
      `the wages I lost each day` IS A NUMBER @desc The wages you lost each day, in dollars
      `the amount already paid to me under s 60A` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Commission has already paid you under s 60A for this accident, in dollars
      `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 44(3)(a) figure (the Act prints $621, varied each 1 July)
      `the current s 60A(4) limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 60A(4) limit (the Act prints $3500)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be paid for wages lost after a later hospital stay` `the day of the accident` `the day I went into hospital` `the days I lost wages` `the wages I lost each day` `the amount already paid to me under s 60A` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the current s 60A(4) limit` MEANS
    IF `s 60A(1)(b) -- the hospital services were at least 3 years after the accident` `the day of the accident` `the day I went into hospital`
    THEN `s 60A -- the most paid for lost wages after a later hospital stay` `the current s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the current s 60A(4) limit` `the days I lost wages` `the wages I lost each day` `the amount already paid to me under s 60A`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Suing for damages: serious injury (s 93)`

-- A situation: only for a person who wants to sue the person at fault for common law damages.

@export Is my injury taken to be a serious injury, so I can sue for damages without the Commission's certificate or a court's leave, because the Commission determined my impairment at 30% or more (s 93(3))? After more than one accident (total over 10%), 30% must come from one of them (s 47(6)(b)).
GIVEN `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined your degree of impairment (under s 46A, 47(7) or 47(7A))?
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree it determined, in per cent (0 if not determined)
      `I was injured in more than one transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that degree come from more than one transport accident?
      `the highest degree from any one of the accidents` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the highest degree from any one of the accidents, in per cent (otherwise the same as your degree)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my injury taken to be a serious injury` `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` `my degree of impairment` `I was injured in more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one of the accidents` MEANS
    `s 93(3) -- the injury is deemed a serious injury` `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` `my degree of impairment` `I was injured in more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one of the accidents`

@export Can I bring proceedings for common law damages for my transport accident injury (s 93(2)-(6))? Only once the Commission has determined your degree of impairment, and either it is 30% or more, or the Commission certifies (or a court gives leave) because it is satisfied the injury is a serious injury. Answers nothing where more than one accident gave 30% or more in total but no one accident gave 30% (the Act does not say).
GIVEN `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined your degree of impairment (under s 46A, 47(7) or 47(7A))?
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree it determined, in per cent (0 if not determined)
      `I was injured in more than one transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that degree come from more than one transport accident?
      `the highest degree from any one of the accidents` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the highest degree from any one of the accidents, in per cent (otherwise the same as your degree)
      `the Commission issued me a serious injury certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission, satisfied your injury is a serious injury (a serious long-term impairment or loss of a body function, permanent serious disfigurement, severe long-term mental or behavioural disturbance or disorder, or loss of a foetus), issued you a certificate consenting to proceedings?
      `a court gave me leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court, satisfied your injury is a serious injury, given you leave to bring the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring proceedings for damages for my injury` `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` `my degree of impairment` `I was injured in more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one of the accidents` `the Commission issued me a serious injury certificate` `a court gave me leave` MEANS
    `s 93(2)-(6) -- the person may bring proceedings for damages for the injury` `the Commission determined my degree of impairment` `my degree of impairment` `I was injured in more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one of the accidents` `the Commission issued me a serious injury certificate` `a court gave me leave`

@export How much can I recover in common law damages for pecuniary loss (lost earnings and earning capacity after the first 18 months) (s 93(7)(a), (11)(a))? Nothing unless the court's assessment is over the threshold; the assessment, or the maximum if it is over the maximum, less the earning capacity payments you received, then reduced for your share of responsibility. Enter the current figures; the Act prints $30 520 and $686 840.
GIVEN `the court's assessment of my pecuniary loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of your pecuniary loss damages, before any reduction for your own responsibility, leaving out loss in the first 18 months after the accident and s 60 expenses, in dollars
      `the earning capacity payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Commission paid you for this injury under ss 49, 50 and 51 (or, if you were not entitled because of s 37, compensation for lost earnings after the first 18 months), in dollars
      `my share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of responsibility for your injury (contributory negligence) as a fraction, e.g. 0.25 for 25%; 0 if none
      `the current s 93(7) threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 93(7) threshold (the Act prints $30 520, varied each 1 July)
      `the current s 93(7)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 93(7)(a) maximum (the Act prints $686 840)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I recover in damages for pecuniary loss` `the court's assessment of my pecuniary loss` `the earning capacity payments I received` `my share of responsibility` `the current s 93(7) threshold` `the current s 93(7)(a) maximum` MEANS
    `s 93(7) -- the damages that can be recovered` `the current s 93(7) threshold` `the current s 93(7)(a) maximum` `the court's assessment of my pecuniary loss` `the earning capacity payments I received` `my share of responsibility`

@export How much can I recover in common law damages for pain and suffering (s 93(7)(b), (11)(b))? Nothing unless the court's assessment is over the threshold; the assessment, or the maximum if it is over the maximum, less the impairment benefit (and minors' benefits) you received, then reduced for your share of responsibility. Enter the current figures; the Act prints $30 520 and $305 250.
GIVEN `the court's assessment of my pain and suffering` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of your damages for pain and suffering, loss of amenities and loss of enjoyment of life, before any reduction for your own responsibility, in dollars
      `the impairment benefits I received` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Commission paid you for this injury under ss 47 and 54 (or, if you were not entitled because of s 37, compensation other than for lost earnings or pecuniary loss), in dollars
      `my share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of responsibility for your injury as a fraction, e.g. 0.25 for 25%; 0 if none
      `the current s 93(7) threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 93(7) threshold (the Act prints $30 520, varied each 1 July)
      `the current s 93(7)(b) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 93(7)(b) maximum (the Act prints $305 250)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I recover in damages for pain and suffering` `the court's assessment of my pain and suffering` `the impairment benefits I received` `my share of responsibility` `the current s 93(7) threshold` `the current s 93(7)(b) maximum` MEANS
    `s 93(7) -- the damages that can be recovered` `the current s 93(7) threshold` `the current s 93(7)(b) maximum` `the court's assessment of my pain and suffering` `the impairment benefits I received` `my share of responsibility`

@export On what day does my cause of action for damages arise, for the time limits of the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (s 93(19))? The accident day, or the day the injury first showed itself if it did not show at the accident. The limitation periods themselves are in that Act, which is not encoded here.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the transport accident (ISO date)
      `the day my injury first showed itself` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury first manifested itself; the accident day if it showed then (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day does my cause of action arise` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself` MEANS
    `s 93(19) -- the day the cause of action arises` `the day of the accident` `the day my injury first showed itself`

§§ `If the person dies (ss 57-60, 93(8))`

-- A situation: asked by the surviving partner, or for a dependent child, of a person who died as a result of a
-- transport accident.

@export My partner died in a transport accident: how much is my lump sum death benefit as a surviving partner (s 57)? The current s 57 figure times (125 - A) / 100, A their age at death (25 to 75); shared with other surviving partners by years of dependency; halved (or less) where dependent children share it under s 57(4); less any impairment benefit paid to them. Nothing if I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death, or was convicted of causing it (s 57(5), (6)). Enter the current figure; the Act prints $103 210.
GIVEN `the current s 57 amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 57 figure (the Act prints $103 210, varied each 1 July)
      `their age at death` IS A NUMBER @desc The age of the person who died, in whole years, at the date of death
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many surviving partners (dependent partners) the person left, counting you
      `the years I was their dependent partner` IS A NUMBER @desc If more than one: the number of years you were their dependent partner (any number otherwise)
      `the other partners' years of dependency, added up` IS A NUMBER @desc If more than one: the years each other surviving partner was their dependent partner, added up (0 otherwise)
      `there are dependent children who share under s 57(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there dependent children who would have had a s 59 death benefit but for a surviving partner being paid (for example children of the person who are not your dependants)?
      `the impairment benefit paid to them` IS A NUMBER @desc Any impairment benefit the person who died received under s 47 for the accident, in dollars (0 if none)
      `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received an award of damages, or made a settlement of damages, in respect of the death (s 57(5))?
      `I was convicted of causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of murder or manslaughter involving the killing of your partner and the use of a motor vehicle, or of culpable or dangerous driving (Crimes Act 1958 s 318(1) or 319(1), or a corresponding law) that caused your partner's death (s 57(6))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my death benefit as a surviving partner` `the current s 57 amount` `their age at death` `the number of surviving partners` `the years I was their dependent partner` `the other partners' years of dependency, added up` `there are dependent children who share under s 57(4)` `the impairment benefit paid to them` `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` `I was convicted of causing the death` MEANS
    IF `ss 57(5), (6) -- the Commission is not liable to pay the s 57 death benefit` `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` `I was convicted of causing the death`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE `s 57 -- the death benefit for a surviving partner` `the current s 57 amount` `their age at death` `the number of surviving partners` `the years I was their dependent partner` `the other partners' years of dependency, added up` `there are dependent children who share under s 57(4)` `the impairment benefit paid to them`

@export My parent died in a transport accident and left a surviving partner who is paid a death benefit: how much is my share as a dependent child under s 57(4)(c)? An equal share of the current s 57 figure divided by (the number of surviving partners + 1). Nothing if I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death, or was convicted of causing it (s 57(5), (6)). Enter the current figure; the Act prints $103 210.
GIVEN `the current s 57 amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 57 figure (the Act prints $103 210, varied each 1 July)
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many surviving partners the person who died left
      `the number of children who share` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children share under s 57(4), counting you
      `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received an award of damages, or made a settlement of damages, in respect of the death (s 57(5))?
      `I was convicted of causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of murder or manslaughter involving the killing of your parent and the use of a motor vehicle, or of culpable or dangerous driving (Crimes Act 1958 s 318(1) or 319(1), or a corresponding law) that caused your parent's death (s 57(6))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my share as a dependent child under s 57(4)` `the current s 57 amount` `the number of surviving partners` `the number of children who share` `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` `I was convicted of causing the death` MEANS
    IF `ss 57(5), (6) -- the Commission is not liable to pay the s 57 death benefit` `I received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` `I was convicted of causing the death`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE `s 57(4)(c) -- each child's share` `the current s 57 amount` `the number of surviving partners` `the number of children who share`

@export My partner, an earner, died in a transport accident: how much is my weekly payment as a surviving partner (s 58)? The greater of 80% of their assessed earnings (what they could have earned in the 12 months after the death, divided by 52) and the minimum for my dependent children, but not more than the maximum or 100% of the assessed earnings; shared by years of dependency with other partners. Nothing for a week after damages for the death were awarded or settled, or if I was convicted of causing the death (s 58(7), (8)). Enter the current figures; the Act prints $304, $85, $27 and $621.
GIVEN `what they could have earned in the 12 months after the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The total the person who died could have earned, but for the accident, in the 12 months after the death in work reasonably available to them, leaving out employer superannuation contributions, in dollars
      `the number of my dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children you have (children of, or dependent on, the person who died, who depend on you and are under 18, or under 25 and studying full-time or apprentices)
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many surviving partners the person left, counting you
      `the years I was their dependent partner` IS A NUMBER @desc If more than one: the years you were their dependent partner (any number otherwise)
      `the other partners' years of dependency, added up` IS A NUMBER @desc If more than one: the other surviving partners' years of dependency, added up (0 otherwise)
      `the current s 58 minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for the minimum with no dependent children, s 58(2)(b) (the Act prints $304, varied each 1 July)
      `the current amount for one dependent child` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for one dependent child (the Act prints $85)
      `the current amount for each other dependent child` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for each other dependent child (the Act prints $27)
      `the current s 58 maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum, s 58(3)(a) (the Act prints $621)
      `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the week you are asking about, was an award or settlement of damages made in respect of the death, by you or anyone else (s 58(7))?
      `I was convicted of causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of murder or manslaughter involving the killing of your partner and the use of a motor vehicle, or of culpable or dangerous driving (Crimes Act 1958 s 318(1) or 319(1), or a corresponding law) that caused your partner's death (s 58(8))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment as a surviving partner` `what they could have earned in the 12 months after the death` `the number of my dependent children` `the number of surviving partners` `the years I was their dependent partner` `the other partners' years of dependency, added up` `the current s 58 minimum` `the current amount for one dependent child` `the current amount for each other dependent child` `the current s 58 maximum` `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the week` `I was convicted of causing the death` MEANS
    IF `ss 58(7), (8) -- the Commission is not liable to pay s 58 weekly payments for the period` `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the week` `I was convicted of causing the death`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE `s 58 -- the weekly payment for a surviving partner`
             (`Weekly payment figures` WITH
                 `the base amount`                     IS `the current s 58 minimum`
                 `the amount for one dependant`        IS `the current amount for one dependent child`
                 `the amount for each other dependant` IS `the current amount for each other dependent child`
                 `the maximum`                         IS `the current s 58 maximum`)
             `what they could have earned in the 12 months after the death`
             `the number of my dependent children`
             `the number of surviving partners`
             `the years I was their dependent partner`
             `the other partners' years of dependency, added up`

@export Until what day are my weekly payments as a surviving partner paid (s 58(5))? Five years after the death or until I reach pension age, whichever is first; but if I then have a dependent child, until I no longer have one. This is the s 58(5) limit only; the bars after damages or a conviction (s 58(7), (8)) are asked in the weekly payment question.
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died (ISO date)
      `the day I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) (ISO date)
      `I will have a dependent child then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the earlier of those two days, will you still have a dependent child?
      `the day I will stop having a dependent child` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you will no longer have one, for example the day your youngest turns 18, or turns 25 or stops full-time study or an apprenticeship (ISO date; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until what day are my weekly payments as a surviving partner paid` `the day of the death` `the day I reach pension age` `I will have a dependent child then` `the day I will stop having a dependent child` MEANS
    `s 58(5) -- the last day of a surviving partner's weekly payments` `the day of the death` `the day I reach pension age` `I will have a dependent child then` `the day I will stop having a dependent child`

@export For a dependent child of a person who died in a transport accident: how much is the child's weekly payment under s 59 on a given day? The current s 59(3)(a) figure until the child turns 18, doubled from 1 November 2026 (s 59(3A)); nothing if a surviving partner is paid and the child is that partner's dependant, after damages for the death, or after the child's conviction for causing it. Enter the current figure; the Act prints $59.
GIVEN `the child's other parent` IS A `The child's other parent` @desc The child's other parent: a dependent partner of the person who died who supports the child; a dependent partner who does not support the child; a parent who is not a dependent partner; or no other parent?
      `the surviving partner later died while paid under s 58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the surviving partner later die (not in a transport accident) while entitled to weekly payments under s 58, the child being their dependent child?
      `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission liable to pay a surviving partner of the person who died a death benefit or weekly payments under s 57 or 58?
      `the child is that partner's dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: is the child a dependant of that surviving partner?
      `damages for the death were awarded or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before that day, were damages for the death awarded or settled?
      `the child was convicted of causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child convicted of murder or manslaughter of the parent involving a motor vehicle, or of culpable or dangerous driving causing the parent's death (s 59(10A))?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth (ISO date)
      `the current s 59(3)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 59(3)(a) weekly figure, before the s 59(3A) doubling (the Act prints $59, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is the child's weekly payment under s 59` `the child's other parent` `the surviving partner later died while paid under s 58` `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` `the child is that partner's dependant` `damages for the death were awarded or settled` `the child was convicted of causing the death` `the day` `the child's date of birth` `the current s 59(3)(a) amount` MEANS
    IF `s 59 -- the payment is payable for the child` `the weekly payment (s 59(3))` `the child's other parent` `the surviving partner later died while paid under s 58` `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` `the child is that partner's dependant` `damages for the death were awarded or settled` `the child was convicted of causing the death`
    THEN `s 59(3), (3A) -- the weekly payment for a child on the day` `the current s 59(3)(a) amount` `the day` (`the day of attaining age` 18 `the child's date of birth`)
    ELSE 0

@export For a dependent child of a person who died in a transport accident: how much is the child's lump sum death benefit under s 59(4)? The current s 59(4) figure divided by the number of dependent children, if the child was under 18 at the death (or under 25 and a full-time student); nothing if a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58 (s 59(9)). Enter the current figure; the Act prints $103 210.
GIVEN `the child's other parent` IS A `The child's other parent` @desc The child's other parent: a dependent partner of the person who died who supports the child; a dependent partner who does not support the child; a parent who is not a dependent partner; or no other parent?
      `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission liable to pay a surviving partner of the person who died under s 57 or 58?
      `damages for the death were awarded or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have damages for the death been awarded or settled?
      `the child was convicted of causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child convicted of an offence causing the parent's death (s 59(10A))?
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children the person who died left
      `the child's age at the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age at the time of the death, in whole years
      `the child was a full-time student at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child a full-time student at the time of the death?
      `the current s 59(4) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 59(4) figure (the Act prints $103 210, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is the child's death benefit under s 59` `the child's other parent` `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` `damages for the death were awarded or settled` `the child was convicted of causing the death` `the number of dependent children` `the child's age at the death` `the child was a full-time student at the death` `the current s 59(4) amount` MEANS
    IF `s 59 -- the payment is payable for the child` `the death benefit (s 59(4))` `the child's other parent` FALSE `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` FALSE `damages for the death were awarded or settled` `the child was convicted of causing the death`
    THEN `s 59(4) -- the death benefit for a child` `the current s 59(4) amount` `the number of dependent children` `the child's age at the death` `the child was a full-time student at the death`
    ELSE JUST 0

@export For a dependent child of a person who died in a transport accident: how much is the child's education allowance a year (ss 59(6), 59A)? The current figure until the child turns 18, under s 59 or, for a child not entitled to it under s 59, under s 59A. Enter the current figure; the Act prints $1660.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth (ISO date)
      `the current s 59(6)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 59(6)(a) figure, per year (the Act prints $1660, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is the child's education allowance a year` `the day` `the child's date of birth` `the current s 59(6)(a) amount` MEANS
    `ss 59(6), 59A -- the education allowance a year for a child on the day` `the current s 59(6)(a) amount` `the day` (`the day of attaining age` 18 `the child's date of birth`)

@export How much does the Commission pay for the funeral of a person who died in a transport accident (s 60(2A)(b))? Its reasonable costs, where the total does not exceed the current figure (the Act prints $14 135). Read as the text stands, a total over the figure gets nothing under this paragraph; it may instead be meant as a cap (see the encoding's notes).
GIVEN `the total reasonable funeral costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The total reasonable costs of the funeral, burial, cremation and monument incurred in Australia, in dollars
      `the current s 60(2A)(b) figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 60(2A)(b) figure (the Act prints $14 135, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much does the Commission pay for the funeral` `the total reasonable funeral costs` `the current s 60(2A)(b) figure` MEANS
    `s 60(2A)(b) -- what is paid for funeral expenses` `the current s 60(2A)(b) figure` `the total reasonable funeral costs`

@export How much can I recover in damages for the death of my family member in a transport accident (s 93(8), (9), (11A))? Damages under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958, less the death benefits paid under ss 57, 58 and 59, and not more than the current maximum (the Act prints $500 000).
GIVEN `the damages assessed for the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages the court assesses for the death under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958, leaving out housekeeping and child care the person would have provided (s 93(12A)), in dollars
      `the death benefits paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Commission paid for the death under ss 57, 58 and 59, in dollars
      `the current s 93(9) maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The current s 93(9) maximum (the Act prints $500 000, varied each 1 July)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I recover in damages for the death` `the damages assessed for the death` `the death benefits paid` `the current s 93(9) maximum` MEANS
    `s 93(8), (9), (11A) -- the damages for a death` `the current s 93(9) maximum` `the damages assessed for the death` `the death benefits paid`
